Validation status and release gates
-----------------------------------

The run6/run8 hardware results recorded in `PORTING-GZIF.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`
(2026-11-17), and every earlier CI run, belong to the **historical
implementation only**: the old multi-marker status protocol, the then-current
`dfroot.ko` pins and the old preference-write path. They predate the rebase
onto the merged PR #1 head. No hardware run validates the current head of
`fix/native-exploit-robustness` (round-5 repair, 2026-11-25); that head is
**host-tested only and UNVALIDATED on device**, and a successful build does not
certify safe privileged execution. run6/run8 and all earlier CI runs, including
45523079469, validate only historical implementations or pre-rebase heads.

- **PR/branch/manual CI artifacts are UNVERIFIED.** Green CI runs execute the
  native/CMake/JVM host suites as required gates and upload a
  debug-keystore-signed Debug APK as a public downloadable Actions artifact
  named `DFRoot-UNVERIFIED-CI`, together with this NOTICE, `GPL-3.0.txt`,
  `LICENSE` and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`. It carries no signed APK, no signing
  secrets, no GitHub Release and no release claim. The all-events gate asserts
  7/7 suite markers (`marker-native`, `marker-ko-policy`, `marker-packaged-ko`,
  `marker-apk-packaging-fixture`, `marker-ko-ci-policy`, `marker-jvm`,
  `marker-junit`), and the strict JUnit XML assertion requires exactly
  **36 tests**, 0 failures/errors/skips (LaunchGate 4, ListenerLifecycle 7,
  PreferenceIntegrity 12, PreferencePersister 13).
- **Publishing gates run before any signed upload or publish.** On the
  protected `v*` tag path only, every distributable APK is packaged-byte-verified
  with a per-APK manifest and `so_sha256` binding; every provenance record gets
  a required identity check (git HEAD, release variant, reviewed KO pin, KO
  manifest and splicehelper binary/source digests, compiler identity); release
  evidence emits one row per uploaded APK, and a distributable-evidence choke
  point gates the signed artifact upload before `publish`. Failed verifier
  reruns cannot leave stale success evidence: manifests and section dumps are
  invalidated at entry.
- **KO pins do not by themselves block a release.** The byte gate rejects
  unknown bytes but **accepts the two known obsolete pins** in
  `app/src/main/jni/CMakeLists.txt`. Release is withheld by **policy** — a
  reviewed re-pin, the OPEN P1-08 staging gate and device validation — not by
  the hash gate alone; passing the gate is not device validation. Skip mode is
  forbidden in CI/release builds. Gradle passes the Android variant
  (`release` / `debug`) as the authoritative native policy signal.
- **Final packaged bytes (no skip).** The KO is linked into a dedicated
  `.dfroot_ko` section; `verify_packaged_ko.cmake` dumps it from
  `libdfroot.so` with objcopy and compares it to the SAME reviewed pins and
  expected sizes. Configure fails without `CMAKE_OBJCOPY`; the gate has no
  skip option and writes a manifest only on success. The protected tag path
  repeats it on every distributable APK before upload. It accepts the known
  obsolete pins, so release is withheld by policy (reviewed re-pin, P1-08,
  device validation) rather than by the gate alone. No tag was created by us.
  Host-only fixture tests are not device validation.
- **Provenance is evidence, not proof or attestation.** The build/provenance
  manifests record hashes, toolchain identity, git HEAD, Android variant and
  KO gate status for auditing, and fail closed on a missing/stale KO manifest;
  they are not an independent reproducible-build proof, and splicehelper is
  not claimed to be bit-for-bit deterministic across toolchains.
- **All CI suites are asserted.** The host suites are **61** status cases plus
  the `final_publish` canonical/permission/atomicity/reader/bootfail/bound+unbound
  recovery checks, 13 proc-scan, 26 ELF and 16+14+10 device-version cases;
  CMake runs 23 KO-policy, 25 packaged-KO, 3 APK-packaging, 3 APK-content and 6
  target-graph cases. Every suite writes a marker that CI checks (7/7 on every
  non-tag CI event), the JUnit XML must report **36 tests** with
  0 failures/errors/skips, and a release-evidence step cross-checks git SHA,
  skip OFF in every CMakeCache, the complete set of verified KO and packaged
  manifests with matching hashes, and every staged APK hash. The publishing
  path adds 3/3 distributable-evidence gates before a single upload choke point.
  The informational provenance upload uses `if-no-files-found: error`; no
  required gate uses `continue-on-error`.

- **PR #1 build/signing baseline (integrated).** Toolchain: Gradle wrapper
  **9.9.2** (distribution SHA-256 pinned), AGP **9.5.0** declared once in
  `gradle/libs.versions.toml` via the version-catalog alias with no root
  `build.gradle.kts` pin, JDK 21, SDK 36, NDK r28c. The single-KMI `make` uses
  the digest-pinned DDK image resolved from CI by `scripts/ddk-image.sh`, with
  `SIGN_PASS`/`SIGN_ALIAS` accepted only from the environment (command-line
  assignments are rejected). Signed releases use a **new key identity**:
  uninstall an existing DFRoot GZIF installation before installing one; the
  UNVERIFIED CI Debug artifact cannot update a signed install either.

> **Post-rebase integration.** PR #1 is now merged into the base; PR #3 was
> rebased onto it. run6/run8 and all prior CI runs are historical and do not
> validate the rebased head. No tag was created by us.

- **App-owned channels and durable preference transaction (host-proven).**
  Bootstrap failures before a run identity exists publish a reserved-nonce
  `BOOTSTRAP_FAILED` token on the separate `dfbootfail` channel (observable
  rc=1, never rc=2); token syntax is not invocation proof. `dfrecover` is a
  strict app-owned recovery status bound to the current run nonce: a stale or
  foreign `ok` is rejected, so syntax alone is not proof of a current cleanup.
  Its poll is bounded to 5 s and clamped to the remaining deadline, and a
  NULL/failed gate or timeout yields `REBOOT_SKIPPED`. The deadline is enforced
  before and after any positive recovery result and after cleanup before a
  terminal outcome; late/uncertain evidence is always `REBOOT_SKIPPED`.
  `status_flow_run()` runs cleanup exactly once on every exit (an `ERR` path
  uses unbound cleanup, the recovery-failed bit and `DF_RC_UNKNOWN`).
  `PreferenceIntegrity` publishes a durable write-ahead `PENDING` marker before
  commit (full write, read-back, fsync), permits recovery only for a fully
  validated PENDING→commit cycle of the SAME key, and latches a sticky
  fail-closed `WILDCARD` on unattributable faults; launch tokens and a
  whole-transaction lock ensure no success is reported for a failed integrity
  transaction, and the boot component is disabled synchronously at the failure
  boundary. Boot component state is tri-state: `UNKNOWN` is never shown as
  verified `OFF` and never used to accept `OFF`, and nothing auto-enables.
  `ExploitRunner` returns rc 9 for `/dev/df` and rc 8 for uncertain preferences;
  `StatusRc` maps rc 0–9 plus the additive 64 recovery bit truthfully. Real
  PackageManager/fsync, asynchronous quiescence and device timing behavior are
  UNVALIDATED; none of this is a substitute for on-device validation.
- **Auto Soft Reboot / Start on Boot remain disabled by default and
  unvalidated** on S9180ZHU8GZIF.
- **P1-08 release gate — still OPEN.** The bundled loaders hardcode
  `/data/local/tmp/.ksud-stage`; race-at-creation is fixed, but a `shell`-uid
  process could still swap the staged file before the loader renames it. This
  cannot be closed without rebuilding the loaders and is a release gate.
  Documenting the gate (or any Java-side gating) is not a fix. Device timing
  and quiescence around the privileged payload stay UNVALIDATED.

